From: LightMoss <lightmoss@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: r36sclone: the blue LED, active high, released when off

The blue front LED that stands in for the rumble motor is active high,
as arkos4clone's led-blue has it: on a G80CA-MB it was lit with gpio0
PA0 driven high at rest, dark with the pin released (as builds that
never touched it left it), and dark with it driven low for an effect.
Driven low at rest it was reported lit too, so between effects the pin
is released rather than driven low: rumble-gpio-hiz-off (the joypad
patch after this). An effect drives it high.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3326-r36sclone-linux.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3326-r36sclone-linux.dts
@@ -67,13 +67,20 @@
 
 		/*
 		 * The G80CA has no rumble motor. Its blue front LED (gpio0 PA0,
-		 * arkos4clone's led-blue) stands in for one, the way spruce blinks
-		 * the LED on the MagicX Zero 28: the driver drives this pin while a
-		 * force-feedback effect plays, so spruce's vibrate (Game Switcher,
-		 * held power/menu buttons, low battery) and game rumble light it.
-		 * Off otherwise, after the driver's 1 s rumble at probe.
+		 * arkos4clone's led-blue, active high) stands in for one, the way
+		 * spruce blinks the LED on the MagicX Zero 28: lit while a
+		 * force-feedback effect plays (spruce's vibrate: Game Switcher, held
+		 * power/menu buttons, low battery; game rumble). Off otherwise, at
+		 * boot and asleep included.
+		 *
+		 * Off is the pin released (an input), as builds that never touched
+		 * it left it. On a G80CA-MB the LED was lit with the pin driven high
+		 * at rest, dark released, and dark driven low for an effect; driven
+		 * low at rest it was reported lit as well, so between effects the
+		 * driver lets go of the pin (rumble-gpio-hiz-off).
 		 */
 		rumble-gpio = <&gpio0 RK_PA0 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		rumble-gpio-hiz-off;
 
 		/* gpio pincontrol setup */
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
